♪ Do you love me at all? ♪

12
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:35,990
♪ Rounding with the little kisses
to my lips before ♪

13
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:42,200
♪ Oh, babe, I want you to be mine ♪

14
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,920
♪ Please do something ♪

15
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:45,890
♪ To show me signs ♪

16
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,680
♪ And make my world to be alright ♪

17
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:51,850
♪ Hold my hand tight ♪

18
00:00:51,870 --> 00:00:53,920
♪ With bright eyes ♪

19
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:57,160
♪ Don't you think
that I belonged to you? ♪

20
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:00,980
♪ Always dominated someone talking to ♪

21
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,690
♪ Oh, you so look like a fool ♪

22
00:01:04,709 --> 00:01:10,800
♪ Finally you have to lose ♪

23
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:18,370
♪ Oh, have to lose ♪

24
00:01:36,729 --> 00:01:39,640
♪ Have to lose ♪

25
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:42,740
[KNOT]

26
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,930
You two are acting like
no one else is here, aren't you?

27
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on Knot]

28
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,560
Nakhun's nose is too sharp.

29
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:52,759
He could find where you were hiding
just by the smell.

30
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,330
It's my fault. I always think too much.

31
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,479
That's right.

32
00:02:18,329 --> 00:02:21,800
[Dad]

33
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,040
Dad.

34
00:02:28,829 --> 00:02:30,230
How have you been, my son?

35
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,920
Dad, you disappeared for a long time.

36
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,829
Don't you miss me?

37
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:39,329
Of course I do.

38
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,590
What father wouldn't miss
his most precious son?

39
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:45,060
Have you been causing any trouble lately?

40
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,400
There was a small incident, Dad.

41
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:59,000
Dad, can I ask you something strange?

42
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:03,030
If it's something you want to know,
just ask me.

43
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:10,230
Dad, do you know about Alpha and Omega?

44
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:14,650
I'm sorry.

45
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:24,060
Where are you right now?

46
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:28,829
I'll come to you right now.

47
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,800
Dad.

48
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:50,340
Phatsa,

49
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:53,530
I miss you so much.

50
00:03:55,650 --> 00:03:57,450
I miss you too.

51
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:04,590
You've grown up.

52
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,460
What's this?

53
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:20,230
I'm asking you. What's this?

54
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:24,160
What's this?

55
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,230
I'm an Omega.

56
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,830
And I've already been marked.

57
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,600
Who did it?

58
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:08,560
Who dared to bite my son?

59
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,430
I'll go and settle the score with him!

60
00:05:10,430 --> 00:05:11,760
How dare he do this to you?

61
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:12,380
Dad.

62
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,360
Calm down.

63
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,220
How can I calm down
when you've already been bonded?

64
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,400
Who do you think is responsible for this?

65
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:32,450
Maybe the one truly at fault is you, Dad.

66
00:05:34,159 --> 00:05:35,700
You never told me anything.

67
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,400
Not about Alphas,

68
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,800
nor Omegas,

69
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:41,860
nor being bitten,

70
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,860
nor being bonded.

71
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:49,920
You didn't tell me anything,
leaving me in the dark.

72
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:52,280
Until all this happened to me.

73
00:05:53,159 --> 00:05:54,800
I'm not blaming you.

74
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,530
I just want to know the truth.

75
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:02,830
Why did you keep it from me all this time?

76
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:19,530
Actually, I'm an Alpha.

77
00:06:22,030 --> 00:06:24,630
I once fell in love with an Omega girl.

78
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:31,100
She was so beautiful that I could never
forget her for the rest of my life.

79
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:35,560
She is your mom.

80
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:44,200
I loved your mom so much.

81
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,930
I loved her too much to bite her.

82
00:06:51,190 --> 00:06:53,320
So I chose to love her with all my heart.

83
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:59,560
Everyone thinks that bonding is
a form of possession.

84
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:02,800
But I know

85
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:07,600
it's really painful for an Omega.

86
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,960
The body aches,

87
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:20,360
and so do the instincts.

88
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:26,320
I couldn't bear to hurt her like that.

89
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:29,360
So I chose not to bite her.

90
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,330
I chose to love her sincerely instead.

91
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:38,700
It wasn't just about an Alpha
and an Omega.

92
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,790
Then one day, I found out

93
00:07:47,730 --> 00:07:49,260
that your mom was pregnant.

94
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,760
I was so happy.

95
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:59,720
I felt like my life was finally complete.

96
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:03,620
But just before you were born,

97
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:08,100
an Alpha enemy of mine

98
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:10,560
bit your mother,

99
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:15,090
and forcibly bonded with her.

100
00:08:15,890 --> 00:08:16,880
Do you know?

101
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,660
At that moment, my world
completely fell apart.

102
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:26,300
Because of that bastard's fangs,

103
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:28,600
I lost everything.

104
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,929
But your mom chose me.

105
00:08:34,059 --> 00:08:35,460
She refused to go with him

106
00:08:36,659 --> 00:08:38,799
and refused to accept that mark.

107
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,860
But the more she resisted,

108
00:08:42,929 --> 00:08:44,660
the more she couldn't stand it.

109
00:08:45,430 --> 00:08:47,490
She was already close to her due date.

110
00:08:49,230 --> 00:08:50,400
I could only stand by

111
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,860
and watch that scene happen
again and again.

112
00:08:56,130 --> 00:08:57,530
I could do nothing.

113
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:03,430
I blame myself every day.

114
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,860
If I had bitten your mom that day,

115
00:09:12,330 --> 00:09:14,700
no one else could have marked her.

116
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:16,630
Or maybe if...

117
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:19,870
If I had let go that day,

118
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:23,800
and let your mom go with the one
who marked her,

119
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:27,060
maybe she would still be alive today.

120
00:09:32,130 --> 00:09:33,990
But no matter how I think about it,

121
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:37,970
in the end, the one at fault is me.

122
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,710
After she gave birth to you,

123
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:45,040
her body finally gave out.

124
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:48,780
Then your mom...

125
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,550
quietly left me,

126
00:09:56,300 --> 00:10:00,170
like a white flower slipping from my hand,

127
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,740
falling into a dark bottomless lake,

128
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:07,730
never to return.

129
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,270
After that,

130
00:10:11,530 --> 00:10:14,030
I sent that bastard to hell
with my own hands.

131
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:17,160
But it could never bring your mom back,

132
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,550
nor stop me from blaming myself,

133
00:10:23,090 --> 00:10:25,020
nor end this nightmare.

134
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,110
I'm sorry, son.

135
00:10:45,790 --> 00:10:46,750
Phatsa,

136
00:10:47,770 --> 00:10:49,200
I really love you.

137
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,160
You look so much like your mom.

138
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:01,610
That's why I'm even more afraid.

139
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:04,390
I'm afraid that being close to you

140
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:09,420
will constantly remind me of the day
I lost your mom.

141
00:11:09,730 --> 00:11:10,960
I let down your mom,

142
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,650
and I let you down too, Phatsa.

143
00:11:19,790 --> 00:11:21,250
That's why I chose to leave

144
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:28,130
and to watch over you from afar.

145
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,190
Because I foolishly thought,

146
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:35,520
that as long as you weren't exposed
to things like Alphas and Omegas,

147
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:38,060
you'll be safe.

148
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:44,930
And I always thought

149
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:47,330
you would be an Alpha.

150
00:11:57,610 --> 00:12:01,530
Because I'm strong, right?

151
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,260
Yes, since you were born,

152
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:12,190
you've been much stronger
than other children.

153
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:13,720
You almost never got sick.

154
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:16,250
You were physically strong,

155
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,050
very smart,

156
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:19,930
with sharp observation skills.

157
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:24,530
And most importantly,
without me teaching you,

158
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:27,810
you could suppress your pheromones
on your own.

159
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:35,000
That's why I always thought you were
an Alpha, just like me.

160
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:42,330
I went for a check-up a while ago.

161
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,660
That's when I found out about Alphas
and Omegas.

162
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,260
At first, I thought I was an Alpha too.

163
00:12:52,330 --> 00:12:54,060
Then I started getting afraid,

164
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:56,000
afraid of becoming an Alpha

165
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:59,780
and accidentally biting someone.

166
00:13:00,230 --> 00:13:02,290
But when the test results came out...

167
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:05,760
I'm not an Alpha.

168
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:12,630
I'm a...

169
00:13:14,230 --> 00:13:15,700
Pure Omega.

170
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:29,560
Pure Omega...

171
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:32,500
I see.

172
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,760
So that's why my Phatsa is so strong,

173
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:37,140
and so smart,

174
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,930
almost like an Alpha.

175
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:46,130
I'm sorry, Phatsa.

176
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,560
It's all because I was too much
of a coward

177
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:56,860
and unable to let go of the past,

178
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,130
that you didn't even know who you were,

179
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:04,200
didn't understand the world of
Alphas and Omegas,

180
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,220
and didn't know how to protect yourself.

181
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:10,330
And in the end,

182
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,360
you got bitten and marked.

183
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:19,960
It's OK, Dad.

184
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,100
There are so many things that are hard
to overcome.

185
00:14:25,730 --> 00:14:29,360
There's always a problem
we can't overcome.

186
00:14:34,860 --> 00:14:35,970
I understand you.

187
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:43,940
Did Mom love me?

188
00:14:51,050 --> 00:14:52,050
Of course she did.

189
00:14:56,840 --> 00:15:00,940
She loved you more than any mother could.

190
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:10,300
Your name Phatsa means rain.

191
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:14,160
When you were born,

192
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:17,100
you carried the scent of rain,

193
00:15:18,570 --> 00:15:19,540
refreshing,

194
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:21,010
gentle,

195
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,190
and bright.

196
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,460
Your mom smelled it on you.

197
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:31,600
That's why she named you Phatsa.

198
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:35,130
Later,

199
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,530
when she was dying,

200
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:40,940
she kept murmuring

201
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,100
your name.

202
00:15:43,950 --> 00:15:44,920
Phatsa...

203
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:47,220
Phatsa...

204
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:54,530
Until the end, she passed away peacefully.

205
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,800
Your mom really loved you.

206
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:05,430
And I love you too.

207
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:58,430
Fated mates...

208
00:18:04,230 --> 00:18:06,090
It doesn't sound romantic at all.

209
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,100
Why?

210
00:18:18,410 --> 00:18:19,710
Why must fate

211
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,960
force us together

212
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,020
when we were total strangers?

213
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:37,260
It's no different from
an arranged marriage.

214
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,560
It's not something we can choose.

215
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:55,500
I always feel like I'm trapped by fate
and the bond.

216
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:01,960
Phatsa,

217
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,760
you're not trapped.

218
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:12,500
I haven't forced you to do anything,
have I?

219
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,830
You haven't forced me.

220
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:24,260
You just want me to stay here.

221
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:39,200
Go get some rest.

222
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,560
Don't overthink things.

223
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,420
Ai.

224
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,070
Lately, I've noticed

225
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,390
Phatsa looks pale,

226
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,740
and seems very tired.

227
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,680
Yes, I've noticed it too.

228
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:24,210
Today, Mr. Phatsa seemed unsteady
on his feet

229
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:26,430
and almost fainted on the stairs.

230
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:34,010
He must be under a lot of pressure.
That's why he's so weak.

231
00:20:34,730 --> 00:20:37,910
Understood. I'll take care of it, Madam.

232
00:20:38,050 --> 00:20:39,420
Very well, I'll leave it to you.

233
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:41,930
OK, I'll get back to work now.

234
00:20:53,230 --> 00:20:54,160
Mr. Phatsa.

235
00:20:54,270 --> 00:20:55,070
Yes?

236
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:56,780
This...

237
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,690
This is a special vegetable and fruit
smoothie.

238
00:20:59,690 --> 00:21:00,990
It's specially made for your health.

239
00:21:00,990 --> 00:21:03,680
It has 17 kinds of vegetables
and fruits inside,

240
00:21:03,710 --> 00:21:06,240
using cold-press technology
to retain all nutrients.

241
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,180
Please try it.

242
00:21:13,630 --> 00:21:14,500
Give it a taste.

243
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:16,620
Hmm!

244
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:21,750
I just ate.

245
00:21:21,970 --> 00:21:23,000
I'm still very full.

246
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,390
Won't you try just a little?

247
00:21:24,390 --> 00:21:25,380
I'm still full.

248
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:27,200
Just a little bit, Mr. Phatsa.

249
00:21:27,430 --> 00:21:28,830
Give it to Jim.

250
00:21:30,230 --> 00:21:31,030
Thank you.

251
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:33,800
What should we do now?

252
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:36,120
Well then, you drink this one.

253
00:21:36,450 --> 00:21:37,250
Please.

254
00:21:37,890 --> 00:21:39,040
Oh my!

255
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:41,230
Oh my, Mr. Phatsa!

256
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,930
Be careful, Mr. Phatsa!

257
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:45,570
Oh, no! This is a disaster!

258
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:46,620
Mr. Phatsa!

259
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:49,090
Be careful. Are you OK?

260
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:52,560
Please just have some.
This is what Madam asked.

261
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:55,810
I'm in a hurry. I have something to do.

262
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:56,900
Just a little bit.

263
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:58,910
Just a little bit, Mr. Phatsa.

264
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:02,890
Just a tiny bit.

265
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:06,460
Jim must be tired.
She said she was hungry earlier.

266
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:08,460
No need. Mr. Phatsa!

267
00:22:08,490 --> 00:22:09,610
Mr. Phatsa.

268
00:22:09,630 --> 00:22:11,760
Drink it. It will keep you energetic.

269
00:22:11,790 --> 00:22:13,120
Drink it now.

270
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:15,270
You have to drink it today, Mr. Phatsa.

271
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,730
Can we drink later?

272
00:22:16,830 --> 00:22:18,560
You said that too yesterday.

273
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:20,270
Just a bit, Mr. Phatsa.

274
00:22:20,290 --> 00:22:23,450
I almost stripped the garden bare
making that juice.

275
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,250
Can you put it in the fridge first?

276
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:28,120
I like cold drinks.

277
00:22:28,590 --> 00:22:30,720
This is already cold.

278
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:33,840
It's freezing...

279
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:35,960
cold!

280
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,450
Right, Mr. Ai?

281
00:22:37,470 --> 00:22:38,130
Yes.

282
00:22:38,130 --> 00:22:40,420
It's freezing cold.

283
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:41,850
Have some, Mr. Phatsa.

284
00:22:41,850 --> 00:22:42,940
Please have some.

285
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,750
Jim, where did you put it?
Is it really that cold?

286
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:46,300
In the backyard fridge.

287
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,680
We don't have any backyard fridge.

288
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,980
I just bought one.

289
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,430
Oh, you bought it yourself.

290
00:22:50,430 --> 00:22:52,010
Yes, I bought it myself.
I have money. Haha!

291
00:22:52,010 --> 00:22:53,600
She has money.

292
00:22:53,630 --> 00:22:57,960
I have money! I bought it myself!
I have money!

293
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:00,880
Mr. Phatsa! Where are you going?

294
00:23:01,230 --> 00:23:02,370
Phatsa!

295
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:03,200
Mr. Phatsa!

296
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,370
Go after him!

297
00:23:05,330 --> 00:23:06,030
Mr. Phatsa!

298
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:11,060
Have some, kid.
You don't look well lately.

299
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:11,960
Well...

300
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,760
I don't really like vegetables.

301
00:23:15,860 --> 00:23:20,160
You have to eat it even if
you don't like it, to be healthier.

302
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:25,410
Just a little, dear.

303
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:32,300
Can I have just a tiny bit?

304
00:23:33,750 --> 00:23:34,810
Finish this glass.

305
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:41,220
Phatsa, I beg you. OK?

306
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:44,170
This will make you healthier. Be good.

307
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:51,510
Drink it up and you'll be healthy.

308
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:59,450
Come on! Come on!

309
00:23:59,470 --> 00:24:01,240
Bottoms up!

310
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:02,770
Come on! Come on!

311
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:08,280
Great. Great!

312
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:15,800
Mom, it tastes too much like vegetables.

313
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:16,660
Just a little more.

314
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:17,440
Mhm.

315
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:19,850
A little more. Come on, go!

316
00:24:19,930 --> 00:24:22,560
Jim, go get Phatsa a glass of water.

317
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:23,660
OK, right away.

318
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,220
Go, go, go, go!

319
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:28,820
Wow, great!

320
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,110
Go, go, go!

321
00:24:35,170 --> 00:24:38,400
Great. You'll be healthy!

322
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:43,750
Drink some water.

323
00:24:44,210 --> 00:24:45,200
Whoa!

324
00:24:45,430 --> 00:24:47,620
Great, good boy. Excellent!

325
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,210
Jim.

326
00:24:49,230 --> 00:24:49,700
Yes?

327
00:24:49,830 --> 00:24:52,170
Where are the lilies I arranged?

328
00:24:52,190 --> 00:24:54,630
-OK.
-Go get them. Let Phatsa feel better.

329
00:24:54,650 --> 00:24:55,630
Hurry up!

330
00:24:55,700 --> 00:24:56,610
Put them here.

331
00:24:56,630 --> 00:24:57,660
So pretty.

332
00:24:57,690 --> 00:25:02,040
The lilies smell wonderful.
They'll help you feel better.

333
00:25:02,470 --> 00:25:07,100
They're so fragrant.
These are specially for you.

334
00:25:10,390 --> 00:25:11,750
Phasta! Oh!

335
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,940
Ai, go check on Phatsa!

336
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:16,790
Yes. Mr. Phatsa.

337
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:23,030
Jim, take Phatsa upstairs to rest.
Don't let him do anything. Hurry up!

338
00:25:30,850 --> 00:25:32,290
So refreshing.

339
00:25:33,510 --> 00:25:36,740
Mr. Phatsa, you're awake.

340
00:25:41,230 --> 00:25:42,960
It's already late, Mr. Phatsa.

341
00:25:43,230 --> 00:25:44,030
Mhm.

342
00:25:44,050 --> 00:25:45,660
I want to sleep a little more.

343
00:25:46,310 --> 00:25:47,910
What's wrong, Mr. Phatsa?

344
00:25:48,460 --> 00:25:49,790
Are you feeling unwell?

345
00:25:49,830 --> 00:25:51,080
Are you OK?

346
00:25:51,590 --> 00:25:52,510
I'm fine.

347
00:25:52,970 --> 00:25:56,430
Then would you like to eat something
and take the medicine?

348
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:59,370
No, thanks, Jim.

349
00:25:59,390 --> 00:26:06,080
Alright then. I'll clean the room quietly.

350
00:26:11,460 --> 00:26:13,660
Jim, could you please not move my stuff?

351
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:21,100
Mr. Phatsa, moving things around
brings more energy to life.

352
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:26,650
It feels like a change of place,
like a new environment.

353
00:26:30,600 --> 00:26:31,400
Huh?

354
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,160
Where's Mr. Phatsa?

355
00:26:34,830 --> 00:26:36,030
He's still sleeping.

356
00:26:36,860 --> 00:26:37,660
Mhm...

357
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:40,150
He looks like he's sick.

358
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:42,650
If Mr. Phatsa really gets sick,

359
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:44,960
Mr. Nakhun will be worried to death.

360
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:47,520
He's been busy with
the Rangsit project lately

361
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:49,180
and hasn't been home for days.

362
00:26:49,460 --> 00:26:52,050
It'll be a real problem if both of them
fall sick.

363
00:26:52,050 --> 00:26:55,250
Mr. Nakhun probably wants to finish
the project as soon as possible.

364
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:56,650
I feel really bad for him.

365
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,070
Speaking of feeling bad,

366
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:02,640
the other day Mr. Phatsa helped
Madam Kampirada arrange flowers,

367
00:27:02,640 --> 00:27:03,660
and he vomited.

368
00:27:03,690 --> 00:27:05,520
He looked so pale.

369
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:10,190
I even told Jim it looked like
pregnancy symptoms.

370
00:27:12,910 --> 00:27:15,280
Oh, could it be...

371
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:23,370
Um, have you been feeling well lately?

372
00:27:24,060 --> 00:27:26,330
I'm fine. Why?

373
00:27:26,350 --> 00:27:28,480
And what about Mr. Phatsa?

374
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:33,870
Have you noticed anything unusual
about him lately?

375
00:27:34,540 --> 00:27:35,330
What's wrong?

376
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:38,540
Phatsa gets tired so easily lately.

377
00:27:38,540 --> 00:27:41,110
He gets nauseous when he
eats something weird.

378
00:27:41,110 --> 00:27:45,220
There are only a few reasons
for these symptoms.

379
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:46,900
Is Phatsa pregnant?

380
00:27:47,590 --> 00:27:49,790
I think so. Probably.

381
00:27:53,060 --> 00:27:54,190
Where are you going?

382
00:27:54,660 --> 00:27:55,900
To see Phatsa!

383
00:28:07,170 --> 00:28:08,350
What are you doing?

384
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,390
What's wrong?

385
00:28:26,950 --> 00:28:27,750
Hm!

386
00:28:29,530 --> 00:28:30,530
What's wrong?

387
00:28:42,070 --> 00:28:43,410
What are you doing?

388
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,320
Get some rest these days.

389
00:29:06,430 --> 00:29:08,090
You should go to bed early too.

390
00:29:10,660 --> 00:29:12,060
I don't want to sleep yet.

391
00:29:13,880 --> 00:29:14,900
I'm happy.

392
00:29:17,950 --> 00:29:18,900
Why?

393
00:29:20,320 --> 00:29:21,720
Is the project finished?

394
00:30:08,820 --> 00:30:09,880
What are you doing?

395
00:30:13,110 --> 00:30:14,080
Drink some more.

396
00:30:36,410 --> 00:30:41,710
Mhm. That's enough. I'll get bloated.

397
00:30:42,810 --> 00:30:43,670
Finish it.

398
00:30:46,100 --> 00:30:47,530
It's good for you.

399
00:30:49,350 --> 00:30:50,150
OK?

400
00:30:51,450 --> 00:30:53,400
I'll really get bloated if I drink more.

401
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:54,690
Then take your time.

402
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:58,630
But you have to finish it.

403
00:31:10,710 --> 00:31:12,420
Aren't you coming up to sleep properly?

404
00:31:12,420 --> 00:31:13,500
Hey!

405
00:31:59,060 --> 00:32:00,660
This old man is quite clingy.

406
00:32:23,790 --> 00:32:26,160
♪ Someday ♪

407
00:32:26,520 --> 00:32:28,950
♪ Bright day ♪

408
00:32:29,050 --> 00:32:34,560
♪ Will conquer us ♪

409
00:32:34,590 --> 00:32:37,450
♪ Someday ♪

410
00:32:37,470 --> 00:32:39,840
♪ The faith ♪

411
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:45,580
♪ Will be about you ♪

412
00:32:56,500 --> 00:32:59,090
♪ Just breathe ♪

413
00:32:59,120 --> 00:33:01,780
♪ Soft tears ♪

414
00:33:02,910 --> 00:33:07,160
♪ The way to be ♪

415
00:33:07,180 --> 00:33:12,460
♪ I'm here, no fear ♪

416
00:33:13,850 --> 00:33:18,400
♪ I'll always be with you ♪

417
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:29,730
♪ I'll always be with you ♪

418
00:33:35,770 --> 00:33:41,300
♪ I'll always be with you ♪

419
00:33:44,610 --> 00:33:46,210
Does this have caffeine in it?

420
00:33:46,210 --> 00:33:54,030
No, only hot water and fresh mint leaves,
as Mr. Ai instructed.

421
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:54,790
Good.

422
00:33:54,810 --> 00:33:55,390
Yes.

423
00:33:55,530 --> 00:33:56,070
Thank you.

424
00:33:56,070 --> 00:33:56,480
Yes.

425
00:33:56,900 --> 00:33:58,430
This is for you, Mr. Phatsa.

426
00:33:58,670 --> 00:33:59,470
Thank you.

427
00:34:06,530 --> 00:34:07,990
Ai, would you like one too?

428
00:34:08,239 --> 00:34:10,260
OK. Thank you.

429
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:13,900
Jim, one for Ai as well, please.

430
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,139
OK.

431
00:34:15,170 --> 00:34:16,159
Thank you.

432
00:34:28,139 --> 00:34:32,710
You've been looking tired lately.
Are you feeling unwell?

433
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:35,810
No.

434
00:34:37,190 --> 00:34:39,159
I've just been sleeping poorly lately.

435
00:34:39,159 --> 00:34:41,350
Have you had any other
unusual symptoms lately?

436
00:34:41,350 --> 00:34:44,820
For example, a particular urge to smell
Mr. Nakhun's pheromones?

437
00:34:44,820 --> 00:34:46,219
A little.

438
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:48,889
I felt weird this morning.

439
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:51,760
My heart was restless for no reason.

440
00:34:51,929 --> 00:34:54,929
But after smelling the scent
on Mr. Nakhun's clothes,

441
00:34:55,030 --> 00:34:56,090
I feel much better.

442
00:34:57,900 --> 00:35:02,100
Is this because of the bond?

443
00:35:10,030 --> 00:35:12,060
Well... It could be.

444
00:35:12,550 --> 00:35:16,610
Usually, bonded partners always want
to smell each other's pheromones.

445
00:35:16,830 --> 00:35:19,430
It makes them feel secure and safe.

446
00:35:20,630 --> 00:35:23,490
Mr. Phatsa, would you like to
video call Mr. Nakhun?

447
00:35:24,660 --> 00:35:25,500
No.

448
00:35:31,700 --> 00:35:32,700
What's wrong?

449
00:35:32,770 --> 00:35:39,120
Nothing. Have some tea.
This helps relieve dizziness.

450
00:35:47,230 --> 00:35:48,030
Where is it?

451
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,360
Why are my clothes here?

452
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:10,750
Is it because you like my scent?

453
00:36:10,750 --> 00:36:11,750
Are you pregnant?

454
00:36:12,530 --> 00:36:13,630
Or are you nesting?

455
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:15,760
Do you nest?

456
00:38:36,130 --> 00:38:37,190
What are you doing?

457
00:38:37,730 --> 00:38:38,730
Did you make this?

458
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:42,030
Is this really edible?

459
00:38:43,290 --> 00:38:44,210
Come on!

460
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:46,560
Don't be picky, Ongsa.

461
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:49,390
I made it myself this morning.

462
00:38:49,410 --> 00:38:50,210
Huh?

463
00:38:51,360 --> 00:38:52,960
You really made it yourself?

464
00:38:55,730 --> 00:38:57,430
I wanted to surprise you.

465
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:01,730
The presentation might be
a little special,

466
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,530
but the taste...

467
00:39:04,430 --> 00:39:05,490
I already tried it.

468
00:39:06,600 --> 00:39:07,630
It should be OK.

469
00:39:08,890 --> 00:39:10,220
It's more than special.

470
00:39:12,220 --> 00:39:13,880
Let me try it then.

471
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:33,610
So salty.

472
00:39:41,970 --> 00:39:43,160
I think...

473
00:39:45,230 --> 00:39:46,330
it's not bad.

474
00:39:49,530 --> 00:39:50,630
Eat first.

475
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,370
Um...

476
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:54,530
I already ate.

477
00:39:55,530 --> 00:39:57,860
I haven't even digested the last meal yet.

478
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:03,300
Well, let's put it in the fridge then.

479
00:40:06,060 --> 00:40:10,600
Good idea. I think it'll taste better
if it's cold.

480
00:40:25,560 --> 00:40:28,560
I'll cook for you every day.

481
00:40:28,850 --> 00:40:32,120
No, thanks. I'm sorry.

482
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:36,750
Nile will be sad.
I can't even eat his food.

483
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:47,590
We still haven't found
that Pure Omega, Master.

484
00:40:52,730 --> 00:40:54,860
They sealed the information tightly.

485
00:40:56,530 --> 00:40:59,130
Even the person who first obtained
the records

486
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:02,430
disappeared during the investigation,
Master.

487
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:05,380
Why can't we find even one child?

488
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:08,490
This Pure Omega is no ordinary person.

489
00:41:09,590 --> 00:41:10,840
Physically strong,

490
00:41:11,150 --> 00:41:13,820
with combat ability nearly equal
to an Alpha.

491
00:41:14,030 --> 00:41:15,190
Most importantly,

492
00:41:15,970 --> 00:41:18,660
they leave no pheromone trail.

493
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,630
So it's hard for us to find them, Master.

494
00:41:23,930 --> 00:41:25,800
If we can't find them,

495
00:41:26,030 --> 00:41:27,560
we should find another way!

496
00:41:29,700 --> 00:41:31,930
Buy records from the hospital.

497
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:33,810
Whatever the cost,

498
00:41:34,530 --> 00:41:36,830
I need to know who that child is.

499
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:40,400
We've already bribed them, Master.

500
00:41:40,940 --> 00:41:44,640
Our people are tracing through
the visitation records.

501
00:41:49,230 --> 00:41:51,630
I want that Pure Omega

502
00:41:52,930 --> 00:41:54,400
to be paired with Nakhin.

503
00:41:55,760 --> 00:41:57,560
No one else must get there first.

504
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:02,020
I'll have this arranged
as soon as possible.

505
00:42:07,990 --> 00:42:10,540
♪ I can see right through your eyes ♪

506
00:42:10,540 --> 00:42:12,900
♪ I can't explain, but it's so clear ♪

507
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:18,970
♪ Even though you try to mumble
through your mask ♪

508
00:42:18,970 --> 00:42:20,870
♪ I still hear you, dear ♪

509
00:42:23,750 --> 00:42:27,690
♪ Sweet honey pie ♪

510
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,230
♪ Let me ♪

511
00:42:29,230 --> 00:42:32,890
♪ Tell you in a way
that you can't understand ♪

512
00:42:32,910 --> 00:42:35,430
♪ No one else is better than you ♪

513
00:42:38,010 --> 00:42:41,030
♪ Charming smile, no wonder ♪

514
00:42:41,030 --> 00:42:43,190
♪ No one else is better than you ♪

515
00:42:45,910 --> 00:42:50,000
♪ Step on it and conquer ♪

516
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:51,170
♪ Only if it's you ♪

517
00:42:51,190 --> 00:42:52,900
♪ It's you, it's you ♪

518
00:42:52,930 --> 00:42:59,370
♪ All I mind, it's you, it's you,
it's you ♪

519
00:43:05,210 --> 00:43:07,140
♪ No one else is better than you ♪

520
00:43:07,170 --> 00:43:08,910
♪ To let others down ♪

521
00:43:08,910 --> 00:43:10,970
♪ You seem to be down, but you're never
willing to live behind others ♪

522
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,300
♪ The one who witnessed your crime
at night ♪

523
00:43:13,330 --> 00:43:19,600
♪ Bury the sin and spread ♪

524
00:43:19,730 --> 00:43:21,530
Why did you bring me here?

525
00:43:21,760 --> 00:43:23,340
♪ I ♪

526
00:43:23,700 --> 00:43:24,900
You'll find out soon.

527
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:42,520
Don't tell me your scent is here.

528
00:43:46,460 --> 00:43:47,460
Smell it.

529
00:44:15,500 --> 00:44:16,360
It smells good.

530
00:44:17,660 --> 00:44:18,460
Do you like it?

531
00:44:26,560 --> 00:44:30,590
I love it. It's really fragrant.

532
00:44:31,050 --> 00:44:32,750
And it's not cloying at all.

533
00:44:35,230 --> 00:44:36,710
When I smell this,

534
00:44:38,040 --> 00:44:39,770
my heart calms down instantly.

535
00:44:44,460 --> 00:44:45,560
This is my scent.

536
00:44:48,300 --> 00:44:49,600
What do you mean?

537
00:44:50,930 --> 00:44:53,730
My pheromones are very close
to this scent.

538
00:44:55,060 --> 00:44:57,860
Even though you can't smell
my actual pheromones,

539
00:44:59,730 --> 00:45:03,360
I want you to know what I smell like.

540
00:45:06,530 --> 00:45:08,360
That's why you brought me here.

541
00:45:10,100 --> 00:45:12,160
I want to be alone with you for a while.

542
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:17,460
Sounds silly, doesn't it?

543
00:45:19,130 --> 00:45:19,930
No.

544
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:24,670
If this really is your scent,

545
00:45:26,700 --> 00:45:28,360
then I'll definitely love it.

546
00:45:35,700 --> 00:45:37,360
I want you to smell this scent.

547
00:45:41,300 --> 00:45:42,260
Why?

548
00:45:44,500 --> 00:45:48,330
So you'll feel like I'm always with you,
holding you.

549
00:45:50,930 --> 00:45:54,460
You're making me shy.

550
00:46:01,960 --> 00:46:02,760
Could it be...

551
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,730
You prepared all of this

552
00:46:10,130 --> 00:46:11,760
so I could know you better.

553
00:46:13,750 --> 00:46:14,550
Yes.

554
00:46:17,550 --> 00:46:18,430
